/* Task 231: the four-category block under the pre-approval master switch —
   a visible risk line plus independent checkboxes (tokens only).
   Task 527: the block is a SIBLING of .settings-field inside
   .autopilot-preapprove-subblock (not a child of the field's control
   column) — a plain block fills the card content width, so the checkbox
   rows and the risk line start at the same left edge as the hint text and
   can no longer be sized by the warning's max-content width (which used to
   spill past the panel edge). */
.set-preapprove {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 6px;
  margin-top: 8px;
}
.set-preapprove__warning {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--warn);
  font-size: var(--text-sm);
  line-height: 1.45;
}
.set-preapprove__row {
  /* B1 (2026-10-03 night dispatch): flex, not inline-flex — each of the four
     categories owns exactly one full-width line under the switch row. */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  color: var(--fg-dim);
  font-size: var(--font-control-small);
  cursor: pointer;
}
.set-preapprove__row input {
  accent-color: var(--accent);
}
/* 任务461-P5 (2026-10-03 用户裁决，覆盖同日 B1 的垂直改法): the pre-approval
   field reads as TWO columns — intro (icon + title + hint) LEFT, on/off switch
   RIGHT (the default .settings-field grid); below the switch, the four
   category checkboxes each own one line and the risk line closes the block on
   its own row. The B1 single-column collapse is gone: it stacked the intro
   above the switch, exactly the layout the ruling reversed. The doubled-class
   specificity (0,2,0) is kept so the later-loaded :where(...) rule in
   SettingsPanel.css cannot squeeze this field back.
   Task 527: since the checkbox block moved out of the control column, only
   the header row (intro | switch) is two-column; the checkbox block below
   spans the full card content width, left-aligned with the hint text. */
.autopilot-preapprove-subblock .settings-field {
  grid-template-columns: minmax(180px, 260px) minmax(320px, 1fr);
  align-items: start;
}
.autopilot-preapprove-subblock .set-seg {
  justify-self: end;
  align-self: start;
}
/* Narrow settings page: fall back to the shared single-column collapse. */
@container settings-page (max-width: 680px) {
  .autopilot-preapprove-subblock .settings-field {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .autopilot-preapprove-subblock .set-seg {
    justify-self: start;
  }
}
